  "question": {
    "text": "The differential equation <math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> represents the arc of a circle&nbsp;in the second and the third quadrant and&nbsp;passing through <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then, the radius (in units) of the circle is&nbsp;"
  },
